# Decodex Agent Discovery

Start every Decodex task by reading `AGENTS.md`. Treat it as the authoritative entry point for repo context, local project skills, and workflow guardrails.

## Skill Loading Order

1. Load the relevant Decodex-specific skill from `.cursor/skills/`.
2. Load community skills from `.agents/skills/` only as supplemental implementation guidance.
3. When instructions conflict, prefer `AGENTS.md` and the Decodex-specific skill over community skills.

## Community Skill Cross-References

| Task | Decodex skill first | Community skill supplement |
|------|---------------------|----------------------------|
| React UI, routes, hooks, Tailwind | `.cursor/skills/decodex-frontend/SKILL.md` | `.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` |
| Browser or E2E verification | `.cursor/skills/decodex-frontend/SKILL.md`, `.cursor/skills/decodex-dev-workflow/SKILL.md` | `.agents/skills/webapp-testing/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/e2e-testing-patterns/SKILL.md` |
| Express APIs, middleware, auth, queues | `.cursor/skills/decodex-backend/SKILL.md` | `.agents/skills/nodejs-backend-patterns/SKILL.md` |
| Shared TypeScript types or strict API contracts | `.cursor/skills/decodex-backend/SKILL.md` or `.cursor/skills/decodex-frontend/SKILL.md` | `.agents/skills/typescript-advanced-types/SKILL.md` |
| STT, alignment, classification, drills | `.cursor/skills/decodex-ai-pipeline/SKILL.md`, `.cursor/skills/decodex-domain/SKILL.md` | `.agents/skills/nodejs-backend-patterns/SKILL.md` only for generic service patterns |

## Reproducible Install

Community skills are locked in `skills-lock.json`. Restore them with:

```bash
npm run skills:install
```

Use `npm run skills:update` only when intentionally refreshing skills from the registry.
